UNAPPLIED DESIGN PATCH — requires Windows build review + acceptance run.
Do not apply to a shipping build without owner approval. It adds an
Authorization header to the existing NSM heartbeat so a *public* NSM
masterlist (tools/nsm-keyservice, NSM_KEY_MODE=public) can verify the
server's NSM key. It changes nothing else: no entitlement, Steam, Cfx
portal, or escrow behavior is touched.

--- a/code/components/citizen-server-impl/src/GameServer.cpp
+++ b/code/components/citizen-server-impl/src/GameServer.cpp
@@
 			HttpRequestOptions ro;
 			ro.ipv4 = true;
 			ro.headers = std::map<std::string, std::string>{
 				{ "Content-Type", "application/json; charset=utf-8" }
 			};
+			// NSM: present this server's NSM-owned key to the NSM
+			// masterlist (never to any Cfx/Rockstar endpoint — this
+			// request only goes to sv_master*/NSM ingress hosts).
+			// Empty (default) => header omitted, current behavior.
+			static auto nsmServerKey = m_instance->AddVariable<std::string>("sv_nsmServerKey", ConVar_None, "");
+			if (!nsmServerKey->GetValue().empty())
+			{
+				ro.headers["Authorization"] = "Bearer " + nsmServerKey->GetValue();
+			}
 			ro.addErrorBody = true;

Operator notes:
  set sv_nsmServerKey "nsm_srv_<id>.<secret>" in server.cfg (keep the file
  private; never commit a real key). Verify against the candidate service:
  valid -> listed; revoked/expired/missing -> rejected and not listed
  (see test matrix in docs/nsm-audit-v077/KEYMASTER-SERVERKEY-AUDIT.md).
